    "title": "Addressing Logistical and Volunteer Challenges in Emergency Distributions",
    "insight": "In Iraq, both flash floods and earthquakes revealed significant logistical and volunteer-related challenges during emergency operations. For the flash floods, the absence of logistical supplies for critical needs like water treatment and distribution led to complications in assisting beneficiary families, exacerbated by adverse weather conditions that posed risks to volunteer safety. Similarly, during the earthquake response, volunteers had to distribute food parcels on foot due to logistical constraints, highlighting planning and execution difficulties. These experiences underscore the need for meticulous logistical planning and robust volunteer support systems to ensure smooth and safe emergency distributions.",
